"MONDO:MalaCards\"}\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/7572\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:0033559\nname: intellectual developmental disorder with seizures and language delay\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0018527\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: nord_rare {source=\"MONDO:NORD\"}\nsubset: omim {source=\"OMIM:619000\"}\nsubset: otar {source=\"MONDO:OTAR\"}\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"IDDSELD\" RELATED ABBREVIATION []\nsynonym: \"SETD1B-NDD\" EXACT ABBREVIATION [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163]\nsynonym: \"SETD1B-Related Neurodevelopmental Disorder\" EXACT [] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/nord\"}\nsynonym: \"SETD1B-related neurodevelopmental disorder\" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163]\nxref: GARD:0018527 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nxref: MEDGEN:1740295 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: OMIM:619000 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: UMLS:C5436574 {source=\"MEDGEN:1740295\", source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0003847 {source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432\"} ! hereditary disease\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/29187 {source=\"OMIM:619000\"} ! SETD1B\nproperty_value: curated_content_resource \"https://www.malacards.org/card/intellectual_developmental_disorder_with_seizures_and_language_delay\" xsd:anyURI {source=\"MONDO:MalaCards\"}\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/8512\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:0035706\nname: SETD2-related microcephaly-severe intellectual disability-multiple congenital anomalies syndrome\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0022397\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: nord_rare {source=\"MONDO:NORD\"}\nsubset: ordo_disorder {source=\"Orphanet:597743\"}\nsubset: orphanet {source=\"Orphanet:597743\"}\nsubset: orphanet_rare {source=\"Orphanet:597743\"}\nsubset: rare\nxref: GARD:0022397 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nxref: MEDGEN:1843293 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: Orphanet:597743 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: UMLS:C5681587 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\", source=\"MEDGEN:1843293\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0002254 {source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4142-7153\"} ! syndromic disease\nis_a: MONDO:0800477 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40006/\"} ! SETD2-related neurodevelopmental disorder without or with macrocephaly/overgrowth\nrelationship: has_characteristic HP:0000006 {source=\"Orphanet:597743\"} ! Autosomal dominant inheritance\nproperty_value: curated_content_resource \"https://www.malacards.org/card/intellectual_developmental_disorder_autosomal_dominant_70\" xsd:anyURI {source=\"MONDO:MalaCards\"}\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/6599\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:0035775\nname: CCNK-related neurodevelopmental disorder-severe intellectual disability-facial dysmorphism syndrome\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0022417\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: nord_rare {source=\"MONDO:NORD\"}\nsubset: ordo_disorder {source=\"Orphanet:600668\"}\nsubset: orphanet {source=\"Orphanet:600668\"}\nsubset: orphanet_rare {source=\"Orphanet:600668\"}\nsubset: rare\nxref: GARD:0022417 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nxref: MEDGEN:1842919 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: Orphanet:600668 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: UMLS:C5681527 {source=\"MEDGEN:1842919\", source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0002254 {source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4142-7153\"} ! syndromic disease\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/1596 {source=\"Orphanet:600668\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4142-7153\"} ! CCNK\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:0054837\nname: intellectual disability, autosomal dominant 57\nsubset: doid {source=\"DOID:0061031\"}\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0025982\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: nord_rare {source=\"MONDO:NORD\"}\nsubset: omim {source=\"OMIM:618050\"}\nsubset: otar {source=\"MONDO:OTAR\"}\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"intellectual developmental disorder, autosomal dominant 57\" EXACT [OMIM:618050]\nsynonym: \"intellectual disability, autosomal dominant 57\" EXACT []\nsynonym: \"mental retardation, autosomal dominant 57\" RELATED DEPRECATED []\nsynonym: \"MRD57\" RELATED DEPRECATED []\nsynonym: \"TLK2-Related Neurodevelopmental Disorder\" EXACT [] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/nord\"}\nsynonym: \"TLK2-related neurodevelopmental disorder\" EXACT [PMID:29861108, PMID:31558842, PMID:34821460]\nsynonym: \"TLK2-related syndrome\" EXACT [PMID:29861108, PMID:31558842, PMID:34821460]\nxref: DOID:0061031 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: GARD:0025982 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nxref: MEDGEN:1648280 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: OMIM:618050 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: UMLS:C4748003 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\", source=\"MEDGEN:1648280\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0015802 {source=\"OMIM:618050\"} ! autosomal dominant non-syndromic intellectual disability\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/11842 {source=\"OMIM:618050\"} ! TLK2\nproperty_value: curated_content_resource \"https://www.malacards.org/card/intellectual_developmental_disorder_autosomal_dominant_57\" xsd:anyURI {source=\"MONDO:MalaCards\"}\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/4521\" xsd:anyURI\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/7256\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:0100525\nname: TCF7L2-related neurodevelopmental disorder\ndef: \"A newly discovered disorder caused by a change (variant or mutation) in the TCF7L2 gene. This mutation may be responsible for developmental delays in childhood, intellectual disability, autism, myopia, ADHD, abnormal physical features and other problems. There is a wide spectrum of severity for individuals affected with TRND. Many of the symptoms of TRND overlap with other neurodevelopmental disorders. TRND must be diagnosed with a genetic test and cannot be diagnosed by symptoms alone.\" [https://rarediseases.org/rare-diseases/145702/, PMID:34003604]\nis_a: MONDO:0700092 {source=\"PMID:34003604\"} ! neurodevelopmental disorder\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/6497\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:0100571\nname: CTNNB1-related neurodevelopmental disorder and/or vitreoretinopathy\ndef: \"Any neurodevelopmental disorder and/or exudative vitreoretinopathy caused by a monoallelic variant in the CTNNB1 gene. Variants in CTNNB1 are related to a neurodevelopmental condition with a broad spectrum of presentations ranging from isolated vitreoretinopathy to a complex neurodevelopmental disorder with mild to severe intellectual disability, microcephaly, spasticity, autism spectrum disorder, and visual defects, including retinal detachment, and abnormal retinal vascularization.\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40006/]\nis_a: MONDO:0003847 {source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432\"} ! hereditary disease\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/2514 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40006/\"} ! CTNNB1\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/7572\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:0100603\nname: FAT4-related neurodevelopmental disorder\ndef: \"Any neurodevelopmental disorder, frequently presenting with lymphatic dysplasia, craniofacial and limb anomalies, and secondary lymphopenia from altered immune cell trafficking, in which the cause of the disease is a variation in the FAT4 gene.\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40065/]\nis_a: MONDO:0700092 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40065/\"} ! neurodevelopmental disorder\nintersection_of: MONDO:0700092 ! neurodevelopmental disorder\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/23109 ! FAT4\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/8778\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:0700281\nname: MYH10-related neurodevelopmental disorder with congenital anomalies\ndef: \"An autosomal dominant complex neurodevelopmental disorder in which the cause of the disease is a mutation in the MYH10 gene.\" [PMID:25003005, PMID:35980381]\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0027145\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: rare\nxref: GARD:0027145 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0100465 {source=\"PMID:25003005\", source=\"PMID:35980381\"} ! complex neurodevelopmental disorder with or without congenital anomalies\nintersection_of: MONDO:0100038 ! complex neurodevelopmental disorder\nintersection_of: has_characteristic HP:0000006 ! Autosomal dominant inheritance\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/7568 ! MYH10\nrelationship: excluded_from_qc_check http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/mondo/sparql/qc/general/qc-single-child.sparql\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/8100\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:0700294\nname: obsolete CTCF-related neurodevelopmental disorder\nproperty_value: IAO:0000231 MONDO:TermsMerged\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9168\" xsd:anyURI\nis_obsolete: true\nreplaced_by: MONDO:0014213\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:0700358\nname: GABRA4-related neurodevelopmental disorder with seizures\ndef: \"A neurodevelopmental disorder caused by variation in the GABRA4 gene. This disorder is characterised by developmental delay, epileptiform EEG abnormalities, and autism spectrum disorder, and/or attention deficit hyperactivity disorder. Other phenotypes observed less frequently include seizures, brain MRI abnormalities, and intellectual disability.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0987-9862, https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/ebi-gene2phenotype, PMID:38565639]\nis_a: MONDO:0700092 {source=\"PMID:38565639\"} ! neurodevelopmental disorder\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/4078 {source=\"PMID:38565639\"} ! GABRA4\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9633\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:0700359\nname: GABRD-related neurodevelopmental disorder with epilepsy\ndef: \"A neurodevelopmental disorder caused by variation in the GABRD gene. This disorder is characterised by developmental delay, generalized epilepsy with atypical absences and generalized myoclonic and/or bilateral tonic-clonic seizures, intellectual disability, and behavioural abnormalities.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0987-9862, https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/ebi-gene2phenotype, PMID:25156961, PMID:34633442]\nis_a: MONDO:0700092 {source=\"PMID:25156961\", source=\"PMID:34633442\"} ! neurodevelopmental disorder\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/4084 {source=\"PMID:25156961\", source=\"PMID:34633442\"} ! GABRD\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9633\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:0700361\nname: RFX3-related neurodevelopmental disorder with autism and other behavioural abnormalities\ndef: \"A neurodevelopmental disorder caused by variation in the RFX3 gene. This disorder is characterised by global developmental delay, intellectual disability, and behavioural abnormalities. Most patients present autism spectrum disorder and/or attention deficit hyperactivity disorder. Other phenotypes observed less frequently include sleep difficulties, micro or macrocephaly, non-specific and non-recurrent dysmorphisms, and brain MRI abnormalities.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0987-9862, https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/ebi-gene2phenotype, PMID:21792059, PMID:25844147, PMID:27525107, PMID:31981491, PMID:33658631, PMID:35982159, PMID:37717291]\nis_a: MONDO:0700092 {source=\"PMID:21792059\", source=\"PMID:25844147\", source=\"PMID:27525107\", source=\"PMID:31981491\", source=\"PMID:33658631\", source=\"PMID:35982159\", source=\"PMID:37717291\"} ! neurodevelopmental disorder\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/9984 {source=\"PMID:21792059\", source=\"PMID:25844147\", source=\"PMID:27525107\", source=\"PMID:31981491\", source=\"PMID:33658631\", source=\"PMID:35982159\", source=\"PMID:37717291\"} ! RFX3\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9633\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:0700362\nname: RFX4-related neurodevelopmental disorder with autism and other behavioural abnormalities\ndef: \"A neurodevelopmental disorder caused by variation in the RFX4 gene. This disorder is characterised by global developmental delay and/or intellectual disability, and behavioural abnormalities including documented autism spectrum disorder.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0987-9862, https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/ebi-gene2phenotype, PMID:25961944, PMID:33658631]\nis_a: MONDO:0700092 {source=\"PMID:25961944\", source=\"PMID:33658631\"} ! neurodevelopmental disorder\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/9985 {source=\"PMID:25961944\", source=\"PMID:33658631\"} ! RFX4\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9633\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:0700363\nname: KDM2B-related neurodevelopmental disorder\ndef: \"A neurodevelopmental disorder caused by variation in the KDM2B gene. This disorder is characterised by speech delay, developmental delay, learning difficulties, and/or intellectual disability. Patients often present behavioral abnormalities including including autism and attention deficit hyperactivity disorder. Other phenotypic features commonly reported include heart defects, unilateral kidney agenesis, ophthalmological anomalies, broad nasal tip, large ear lobes, and exaggerated Cupid’s bow.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0987-9862, https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/ebi-gene2phenotype, PMID:36322151]\nis_a: MONDO:0700092 {source=\"PMID:36322151\"} ! neurodevelopmental disorder\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/13610 {source=\"PMID:36322151\"} ! KDM2B\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9633\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:0700364\nname: TRA2B-related neurodevelopmental disorder\ndef: \"A neurodevelopmental disorder caused by variation in the TRA2B gene. This disorder is characterised by intellectual disability and/or developmental delay, with delayed or absent speech and delayed motor development. Most patients present axial or global hypotonia in the neonatal to infancy period, and brain MRI abnormalities. Other phenotypic features commonly reported include infantile spasms, microcephaly, variable behavioral abnormalities, feeding difficulties, and short stature.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0987-9862, https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/ebi-gene2phenotype, PMID:36549593]\nis_a: MONDO:0700092 {source=\"PMID:36549593\"} ! neurodevelopmental disorder\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/10781 {source=\"PMID:36549593\"} ! TRA2B\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9633\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:0700365\nname: WDR5-related neurodevelopmental disorder\ndef: \"A neurodevelopmental disorder caused by variation in the WDR5 gene. This disorder is characterised by speech and language delay, motor development delay and/or intellectual disability. Other phenotypic features commonly reported include hypotonia, epilepsy, and behavioural abnormalities.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0987-9862, https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/ebi-gene2phenotype, PMID:36408368]\nis_a: MONDO:0700092 {source=\"PMID:36408368\"} ! neurodevelopmental disorder\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/12757 {source=\"PMID:36408368\"} ! WDR5\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9633\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:0700366\nname: ARF3-related neurodevelopmental disorder\ndef: \"A neurodevelopmental disorder caused by variation in the ARF3 gene. This disorder is characterised by intellectual disability, delayed or absent speech, motor development delay, and brain MRI abnormalitites. Other phenotypes observed less frequently include seizures, hypotonia, acquired microcephaly, dysmorphic features, and cardiac abnormalities.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0987-9862, https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/ebi-gene2phenotype, PMID:36369169]\nis_a: MONDO:0700092 {source=\"PMID:36369169\"} ! neurodevelopmental disorder\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/654 {source=\"PMID:36369169\"} ! ARF3\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9633\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:0700367\nname: CBX1-related neurodevelopmental disorder\ndef: \"A neurodevelopmental disorder caused by variation in the CBX1 gene. This disorder is characterised by global motor and language developmental delay, intellectual disability, hypotonia, autism spectrum disorder, and variable dysmorphic features.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0987-9862, https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/ebi-gene2phenotype, PMID:37087635]\nis_a: MONDO:0700092 {source=\"PMID:37087635\"} ! neurodevelopmental disorder\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/1551 {source=\"PMID:37087635\"} ! CBX1\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9633\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:0700368\nname: DDX17-related neurodevelopmental disorder\ndef: \"A neurodevelopmental disorder caused by variation in the DDX17 gene. This disorder is characterised by global developmental, motor, language and speech delay, and intellectual disability. Other phenotypic features commonly reported include hypotonia, dysmorphic facial features, behavioural abnormalities, mainly attention deficit hyperactivity disorder, and brain MRI abnormalities.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0987-9862, https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/ebi-gene2phenotype, PMID:39405200]\nis_a: MONDO:0700092 {source=\"PMID:39405200\"} ! neurodevelopmental disorder\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/2740 {source=\"PMID:39405200\"} ! DDX17\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9633\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:0700369\nname: FEZF2-related neurodevelopmental disorder\ndef: \"A neurodevelopmental disorder caused by variation in the FEZF2 gene. This disorder is characterised by developmental delay, intellectual disability, autism spectrum disorder, and/or attention deficit hyperactivity disorder.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0987-9862, https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/ebi-gene2phenotype, PMID:38425142]\nis_a: MONDO:0700092 {source=\"PMID:38425142\"} ! neurodevelopmental disorder\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/13506 {source=\"PMID:38425142\"} ! FEZF2\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9633\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:0700370\nname: HDAC3-related neurodevelopmental disorder\ndef: \"A neurodevelopmental disorder caused by variation in the HDAC3 gene. This disorder is characterised by intellectual disability and neurodevelopmental delay. Phenotypes commonly reported include musculoskeletal abnormalities, abnormalities of the genitourinary system, and brain imaging abnormalities. Other phenotypes observed less frequently include microcephaly, hearing impairments, congenital heart disease, and autistic behavior.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0987-9862, https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/ebi-gene2phenotype, PMID:39047730]\nis_a: MONDO:0700092 {source=\"PMID:39047730\"} ! neurodevelopmental disorder\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/10781 {source=\"PMID:39047730\"} ! TRA2B\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9633\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:0800456\nname: SYNCRIP-related neurodevelopmental disorder\ndef: \"Any neurodevelopmental disorder in which the cause of the disease is a variation in the SYNCRIP gene. It is characterized by a neurologic and developmental disorder with autism spectrum disorder (ASD), intellectual disability (ID), and epilepsy. Other signs and symptoms may include cerebral structural anomalies such as periventricular nodular heterotopia and widening of subarachnoid spaces.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163, MONDO:patterns/disease_series_by_gene, PMID:34157790]\nis_a: MONDO:0100500 {source=\"PMID:34157790\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163\"} ! Mendelian neurodevelopmental disorder\nintersection_of: MONDO:0700092 ! neurodevelopmental disorder\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/16918 ! SYNCRIP\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/6965\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:0800457\nname: HNRNPC-related neurodevelopmental disorder\ndef: \"Any neurodevelopmental disorder in which the cause of the disease is a variation in the HNRNPC gene. It is characterized by global developmental delay, intellectual disability, behavioral abnormalities, and subtle facial dysmorphism. It is caused by heterozygous HNRNPC germline variants.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163, MONDO:patterns/disease_series_by_gene, PMID:37541189]\nis_a: MONDO:0100500 {source=\"PMID:37541189\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163\"} ! Mendelian neurodevelopmental disorder\nintersection_of: MONDO:0700092 ! neurodevelopmental disorder\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/5035 ! HNRNPC\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/6964\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:0800475\nname: NACC1-related neurodevelopmental disorder with epilepsy, cataracts and episodic irritability\ndef: \"A neurodevelopmental disorder caused by heterozygous variants in NACC1 and characterized by developmental delay, intellectual disability, epilepsy, cataracts, feeding difficulties, and recurring episodes of extreme irritability. Other phenotypes include hypotonia, delayed myelination, microcephaly, stereotypic hand movements, gastrointestinal tract issues, and sleeping problems.\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40006/]\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0027073\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"NACC1-related neurodevelopmental disorder with epilepsy, cataracts and episodic irritability\" EXACT [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40006/] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nxref: GARD:0027073 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0001071 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40006/\"} ! intellectual disability\nis_a: MONDO:0100038 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40006/\"} ! complex neurodevelopmental disorder\nis_a: MONDO:0700092 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40006/\"} ! neurodevelopmental disorder\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/20967 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40006/\"} ! NACC1\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/6700\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:0800477\nname: SETD2-related neurodevelopmental disorder without or with macrocephaly/overgrowth\ndef: \"A neurodevelopmental disorder caused by heterozygous variants in SETD2 and characterized by intellectual disability or developmental delay, motor delay, speech delay, hypotonia, autism spectrum disorder, attention deficit disorder, and sometimes features such as macrocephaly, overgrowth, and dysmorphic features.\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40006/]\nsynonym: \"SETD2-related neurodevelopmental disorder without or with macrocephaly/overgrowth\" EXACT [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40006/] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0001071 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40006/\"} ! intellectual disability\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/18420 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40006/\"} ! SETD2\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/6599\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:0859143\nname: Radio-Tartaglia syndrome\ndef: \"A syndrome that is caused by a variation in the SPEN gene and is characterized by developmental delay/intellectual disability, autism spectrum disorder, anxiety, aggressive behavior, attention deficit disorder, hypotonia, brain and spine anomalies, congenital heart defects, high/narrow palate, facial dysmorphisms, and obesity/increased BMI, especially in females.\" [PMID:33596411]\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0027075\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: omim {source=\"OMIM:619312\"}\nsubset: ordo_disorder {source=\"Orphanet:662234\"}\nsubset: orphanet {source=\"Orphanet:662234\"}\nsubset: orphanet_rare {source=\"Orphanet:662234\"}\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"SPEN-related neurodevelopmental disorder\" EXACT [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40060/, Orphanet:662234]\nxref: GARD:0027075 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nxref: MEDGEN:1778557 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: OMIM:619312 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: Orphanet:662234 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: UMLS:C5543339 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\", source=\"MEDGEN:1778557\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0003847 {source=\"OMIM:619312\"} ! hereditary disease\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/17575 {source=\"OMIM:619312\"} ! SPEN\nproperty_value: curated_content_resource \"https://www.malacards.org/card/radio_tartaglia_syndrome\" xsd:anyURI {source=\"MONDO:MalaCards\"}\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/6860\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:0859152\nname: neurodevelopmental disorder with cerebellar atrophy and motor dysfunction\ndef: \"A neurodevelopmental disorder caused by variation in the GEMIN5 gene, characterized by global developmental delay with prominent motor abnormalities, mainly axial hypotonia, gait ataxia, and appendicular spasticity.\" [OMIM:619333, PMID:33963192, PMID:38773790]\ncomment: Affected individuals have cognitive impairment and speech delay; brain imaging shows cerebellar atrophy. The severity is variable. Other symptoms described include early‐infantile developmental and epileptic encephalopathies.\nsubset: doid {source=\"DOID:0070443\"}\nsubset: omim {source=\"OMIM:619333\"}\nsynonym: \"GEMIN5 disorder\" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163, PMID:38773790]\nsynonym: \"GEMIN5-related neurodevelopmental disorder\" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163, PMID:33963192]\nsynonym: \"NEDCAM\" EXACT ABBREVIATION [OMIM:619333]\nxref: DOID:0070443 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: MEDGEN:1781936 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: OMIM:619333 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: UMLS:C5543427 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MEDGEN:1781936\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0700092 {source=\"OMIM:619333\"} ! neurodevelopmental disorder\nintersection_of: MONDO:0700092 ! neurodevelopmental disorder\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/20043 ! GEMIN5\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/20043 {source=\"OMIM:619333\"} ! GEMIN5\nproperty_value: curated_content_resource \"https://www.malacards.org/card/neurodevelopmental_disorder_with_cerebellar_atrophy_and_motor_dysfunction\" xsd:anyURI {source=\"MONDO:MalaCards\"}\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9862\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:0859190\nname: neurodevelopmental-craniofacial syndrome with variable renal and cardiac abnormalities\nsubset: omim {source=\"OMIM:619522\"}\nsynonym: \"ZMYM2-related neurodevelopmental disorder with multiple anomalies\" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163]\nxref: MEDGEN:1794194 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: OMIM:619522 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: UMLS:C5561984 {source=\"MEDGEN:1794194\", source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0003847 {source=\"OMIM:619522\"} ! hereditary disease\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/12989 {source=\"OMIM:619522\"} ! ZMYM2\nproperty_value: curated_content_resource \"https://www.malacards.org/card/neurodevelopmental_craniofacial_syndrome_with_variable_renal_and_cardiac_abnormalities\" xsd:anyURI {source=\"MONDO:MalaCards\"}\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:0859262\nname: ACCES syndrome\ndef: \"A rare congenital disease caused by a mutation in the UBA2 gene, charcterized by scalp defects, digital and skeletal anomalies, early growth deficiency, and neurodevelopmental delay. Ectrodactyly presents in some cases.\" [OMIM:619959]\nsubset: omim {source=\"OMIM:619959\"}\nsynonym: \"aplasia cutis congenita with ectrodactyly skeletal syndrome\" EXACT [OMIM:619959]\nsynonym: \"UBA2-related neurodevelopmental disorder, aplasia cutis congenita with ectrodactyly skeletal syndrome\" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163, PMID:34040189]\nxref: MEDGEN:1804308 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: OMIM:619959 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: UMLS:C5677019 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\", source=\"MEDGEN:1804308\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0003847 {source=\"OMIM:619959\"} ! hereditary disease\nintersection_of: MONDO:0003847 ! hereditary disease\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/30661 ! UBA2\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/30661 {source=\"OMIM:619959\"} ! UBA2\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9464\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:0859333\nname: intellectual developmental disorder, autosomal dominant 70\nsubset: doid {source=\"DOID:0061043\"}\nsubset: omim {source=\"OMIM:620157\"}\nxref: DOID:0061043 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: MEDGEN:1824044 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: OMIM:620157 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: UMLS:C5774271 {source=\"MEDGEN:1824044\", source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0100172 {source=\"OMIM:620157\"} ! intellectual disability, autosomal dominant\nis_a: MONDO:0800477 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40006/\"} ! SETD2-related neurodevelopmental disorder without or with macrocephaly/overgrowth\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/18420 {source=\"OMIM:620157\"} ! SETD2\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/6599\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:0957397\nname: intellectual developmental disorder, autosomal dominant 72\ndef: \"An autosomal dominant intellectual disability disorder characterized by developmental delay, predominant speech delay, autistic or attention-deficit/hyperactivity disorder features, overfriendliness, generalized hypotonia, overweight/obesity, and dysmorphic features.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163, OMIM:620439, Orphanet:652487, PMID:35567594, PMID:37272925]\nsubset: doid {source=\"DOID:0061045\"}\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0026821\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: omim {source=\"OMIM:620439\"}\nsubset: ordo_disorder {source=\"Orphanet:652487\"}\nsubset: orphanet {source=\"Orphanet:652487\"}\nsubset: orphanet_rare {source=\"Orphanet:652487\"}\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"autosomal dominant intellectual developmental disorder-72\" EXACT []\nsynonym: \"developmental delay-overweight-facial dysmorphism-behavioral abnormalities syndrome\" EXACT [Orphanet:652487]\nsynonym: \"MRD72\" EXACT ABBREVIATION [OMIM:620439]\nsynonym: \"SRRM2-related neurodevelopmental disorder\" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163]\nxref: DOID:0061045 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: GARD:0026821 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nxref: MEDGEN:1841248 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: OMIM:620439 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: Orphanet:652487 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: UMLS:C5830612 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\", source=\"MEDGEN:1841248\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0100172 {source=\"OMIM:620439\"} ! intellectual disability, autosomal dominant\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/16639 {source=\"OMIM:620439\"} ! SRRM2\nproperty_value: curated_content_resource \"https://www.malacards.org/card/intellectual_developmental_disorder_autosomal_dominant_72\" xsd:anyURI {source=\"MONDO:MalaCards\"}\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:0958071\nname: Hao-Fountain syndrome due to USP7 mutation\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0026917\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: omim {source=\"OMIM:616863\"}\nsubset: ordo_subtype_of_a_disorder {source=\"Orphanet:643538\"}\nsubset: orphanet {source=\"Orphanet:643538\"}\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"USP7-related neurodevelopmental disorder\" EXACT [https://www.clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40060/] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nxref: GARD:0026917 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nxref: MEDGEN:1853151 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: OMIM:616863 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: Orphanet:643538 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: UMLS:C5816734 {source=\"MEDGEN:1853151\", source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0014805 {source=\"Orphanet:643538\"} ! Hao-Fountain syndrome\nintersection_of: MONDO:0014805 ! Hao-Fountain syndrome\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/12630 ! USP7\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/12630 {source=\"OMIM:616863\"} ! USP7\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:0968978\nname: aplasia cutis-enamel dysplasia syndrome\nsubset: omim {source=\"OMIM:620789\"}\nsubset: ordo_disorder {source=\"Orphanet:697356\"}\nsubset: orphanet {source=\"Orphanet:697356\"}\nsubset: orphanet_rare {source=\"Orphanet:697356\"}\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"Congenital scalp aplasia cutis-enamel hypoplasia-developmental delay-intellectual disability syndrome\" EXACT [Orphanet:697356]\nsynonym: \"FOSL2-related neurodevelopmental disorder\" EXACT [Orphanet:697356]\nxref: MEDGEN:1854704 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: OMIM:620789 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: Orphanet:697356 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: UMLS:C5935608 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\", source=\"MEDGEN:1854704\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0000508 {source=\"Orphanet:697356\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4142-7153\"} ! syndromic intellectual disability\nis_a: MONDO:0002254 {source=\"OMIM:620789\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4142-7153\"} ! syndromic disease\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/3798 {source=\"OMIM:620789\"} ! FOSL2\nproperty_value: curated_content_resource \"https://www.malacards.org/card/aplasia_cutis_enamel_dysplasia_syndrome\" xsd:anyURI {source=\"MONDO:MalaCards\"}\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:0971172\nname: neurodevelopmental disorder with hypotonia, brain anomalies, distinctive facies, and absent language\ndef: \"A syndromic neurodevelopmental disorder in which the cause of the disease is a variation in RNU4-2 gene and is inherited in an autosomal dominant pattern. It is characterized by moderate to severe global developmental delay/intellectual disability, speech anomalies (mostly non-verbal), hypotonia, abnormal brain MRI (reduced white matter volume, hypoplasia of the corpus callosum, ventriculomegaly, and delayed myelination), dysmorphic facial features, short stature, microcephaly, behavioral issues, seizures and feeding difficulties, as well as variable vision, gastrointestinal, endocrine, skeletal, genitourinary, cardiac, and cutaneous anomalies. It has autosomal dominant inheritance.\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40060/, PMID:38821540, PMID:38991538, PMID:40379786]\nsubset: doid {source=\"DOID:0061190\"}\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0027315\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: omim {source=\"OMIM:620851\"}\nsubset: ordo_disorder {source=\"Orphanet:686488\"}\nsubset: orphanet {source=\"Orphanet:686488\"}\nsubset: orphanet_rare {source=\"Orphanet:686488\"}\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"NEDHAFA\" EXACT ABBREVIATION [OMIM:620851]\nsynonym: \"RENU\" EXACT ABBREVIATION [OMIM:620851]\nsynonym: \"ReNU syndrome\" EXACT [DOID:0061190, OMIM:620851, Orphanet:686488]\nsynonym: \"RNU4-2-related neurodevelopmental disorder-facial dysmorphism-white matter abnormalities-short stature syndrome\" EXACT [Orphanet:686488, PMID:38645094, PMID:38821540]\nsynonym: \"RNU4-2-related neurodevelopmental syndrome\" EXACT [Orphanet:686488, PMID:38645094, PMID:38821540]\nsynonym: \"RNU4-2-related ReNU syndrome\" EXACT [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40060/] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nxref: DOID:0061190 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: GARD:0027315 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nxref: MEDGEN:1854654 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: OMIM:620851 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: Orphanet:686488 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: UMLS:C5935628 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\", source=\"MEDGEN:1854654\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0003847 {source=\"OMIM:620851\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4142-7153\"} ! hereditary disease\nis_a: MONDO:0100500 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40060/\"} ! Mendelian neurodevelopmental disorder\nis_a: MONDO:0700092 {source=\"OMIM:620851\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4142-7153\"} ! neurodevelopmental disorder\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/10193 {source=\"OMIM:620851\"} ! RNU4-2\nproperty_value: curated_content_resource \"https://www.malacards.org/card/renu_syndrome\" xsd:anyURI {source=\"MONDO:MalaCards\"}\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/8496\" xsd:anyURI\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9547\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1010145\nname: PIP5K1C-related neurodevelopmental disorder\ndef: \"Any neurodevelopmental disorder in which the cause of the disease is a monoallelic gain-of-function variation in the PIP5K1C gene leading to increased levels of phosphatidylinositol 4,5 bisphosphate. This disorder is characterized by intellectual disability, motor and speech delay, microcephaly, seizures, visual and ocular abnormalities, and craniofacial dysmorphic features.\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40006/, PMID:37451268]\ncomment: This is a distinct entity from MONDO:0012656 lethal congenital contractural syndrome 3.\nsynonym: \"PIP5K1C-related neurodevelopmental disorder\" EXACT [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40006/] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0700092 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40006/\"} ! neurodevelopmental disorder\nintersection_of: MONDO:0700092 ! neurodevelopmental disorder\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/8996 ! PIP5K1C\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/8996 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40006/\"} ! PIP5K1C\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/8931\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1040003\nname: KCND2-related neurodevelopmental disorder with or without seizures\ndef: \"A neurodevelopmental disorder caused by variation in the KCND2 gene. This disorder is characterized by early-onset global developmental delay with impaired motor, speech and cognitive development. Patients often present muscle hypotonia, and less frequently, developmental epileptic encephalopathy, visual impairment and physical dysmorphisms.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0587-4693, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0987-9862, PMID:34245260]\nis_a: MONDO:0100500 {source=\"PMID:34245260\"} ! Mendelian neurodevelopmental disorder\nis_a: MONDO:0700092 {source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0987-9862\"} ! neurodevelopmental disorder\nintersection_of: MONDO:0700092 ! neurodevelopmental disorder\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/6238 ! KCND2\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0587-4693\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/8155\" xsd:string\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/8489\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1040005\nname: PRPF19-related neurodevelopmental disorder\ndef: \"Any neurodevelopmental disorder in which the cause of the disease is a mutation in the PRPF19 gene. This disorder is characterised by developmental, motor and speech delay, and facial dysmorphisms. Most patients present mild to moderate intellectual disability, autism spectrum disorder or autistic features, and hypotonia. Other phenotypes observed less frequently include seizures, and visual and cardiac abnormalities.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0587-4693, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0987-9862, PMID:37962958]\nis_a: MONDO:0100500 {source=\"PMID:37962958\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0587-4693\"} ! Mendelian neurodevelopmental disorder\nis_a: MONDO:0700092 {source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0987-9862\"} ! neurodevelopmental disorder\nintersection_of: MONDO:0100500 ! Mendelian neurodevelopmental disorder\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/17896 ! PRPF19\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0587-4693\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/8156\" xsd:string\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/8489\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1040006\nname: CTR9-related neurodevelopmental disorder\ndef: \"Any neurodevelopmental disorder in which the cause of the disease is a variation in the CTR9 gene. This disorder is characterised by varying degrees of intellectual disability, neurodevelopmental delay, hypotonia, fatigability, behavioral abnormalities including autism spectrum disorder, anxiety and aggressive behavior, cardiac anomalies, and mild facial dysmorphism.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0587-4693, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0987-9862, PMID:35468861, PMID:35499524, PMID:35717577]\nis_a: MONDO:0100500 {source=\"PMID:35468861\", source=\"PMID:35499524\", source=\"PMID:35717577\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0587-4693\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0987-9862\"} ! Mendelian neurodevelopmental disorder\nis_a: MONDO:0700092 {source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0987-9862\"} ! neurodevelopmental disorder\nintersection_of: MONDO:0100500 ! Mendelian neurodevelopmental disorder\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/16850 ! CTR9\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0587-4693\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/8157\" xsd:string\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/8489\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1040008\nname: CAMK2D-related neurodevelopmental disorder and dilated cardiomyopathy\ndef: \"A neurodevelopmental disorder caused by variation in the CAMK2D gene. This disorder is characterised by intellectual disability, speech and motor delay, behavioural problems and dilated cardiomyopathy. Patients often present brain structural anomalies and hypotonia, and less frequently, seizures.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0587-4693, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0987-9862, PMID:37372357, PMID:38272033]\nis_a: MONDO:0100500 {source=\"PMID:37372357\", source=\"PMID:38272033\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0587-4693\"} ! Mendelian neurodevelopmental disorder\nis_a: MONDO:0700092 {source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0987-9862\"} ! neurodevelopmental disorder\nintersection_of: MONDO:0100500 ! Mendelian neurodevelopmental disorder\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/1462 ! CAMK2D\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0587-4693\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/8158\" xsd:string\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/8489\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1040014\nname: PPFIA3-related neurodevelopmental disorder\ndef: \"A neurodevelopmental disorder caused by variation in the PPFIA3 gene. This disorder is characterised by developmental delay and intellectual disability. Most patients present variable additional features, including dysmorphisms, microcephaly or macrocephaly, hypotonia, autism spectrum disorder or autistic features, abnormal electroencephalogram, and epilepsy.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0587-4693, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0987-9862, PMID:38181735]\nsubset: omim {source=\"OMIM:621122\"}\nxref: OMIM:621122 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0100500 {source=\"PMID:38181735\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0587-4693\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0987-9862\"} ! Mendelian neurodevelopmental disorder\nis_a: MONDO:0700092 {source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0987-9862\"} ! neurodevelopmental disorder\nintersection_of: MONDO:0100500 ! Mendelian neurodevelopmental disorder\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/9247 ! PPFIA3\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/9247 {source=\"OMIM:621122\"} ! PPFIA3\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0587-4693\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/8160\" xsd:string\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/8489\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060108\nname: PURA-related severe neonatal hypotonia-seizures-encephalopathy syndrome\ndef: \"A rare neurologic disease characterized by neonatal hypotonia, global developmental delay, feeding difficulties, and often seizures or seizure-like episodes. Other frequently observed signs and symptoms include variable dysmorphic features, myopathic facies, respiratory problems, and visual abnormalities, such as strabismus or esotropia. Brain imaging may show delayed myelination and other white matter abnormalities.\" [Orphanet:438213]\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0027440\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: ordo_disorder {source=\"Orphanet:438213\"}\nsubset: orphanet {source=\"Orphanet:438213\"}\nsubset: orphanet_rare {source=\"Orphanet:438213\"}\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"PURA syndrome\" NARROW [PMID:28448108]\nsynonym: \"PURA-related neurodevelopmental disorders\" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163, PMID:28448108]\nxref: GARD:0027440 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nxref: ICD10CM:G40.4 {source=\"Orphanet:438213\"}\nxref: MEDGEN:863794 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: Orphanet:438213 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: UMLS:C4015357 {source=\"MEDGEN:863794\", source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0003847 {source=\"PMID:28448108\"} ! hereditary disease\nis_a: MONDO:0015159 {source=\"Orphanet:438213\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163\"} ! multiple congenital anomalies/dysmorphic syndrome-intellectual disability\nrelationship: curated_content_resource https://www.malacards.org/card/pura_related_neurodevelopmental_disorders {source=\"MONDO:MalaCards\"}\nrelationship: has_characteristic HP:0000006 {source=\"Orphanet:438213\"} ! Autosomal dominant inheritance\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/5114\" xsd:anyURI\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/6695\" xsd:anyURI\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/6752\" xsd:anyURI\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/6876\" xsd:anyURI\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/6878\" xsd:anyURI\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/8953\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060123\nname: GRIN1-related complex neurodevelopmental disorder\ndef: \"A neurodevelopmental disorder caused by variation in the GRIN1 gene. It is characterized by mild-to-profound developmental delay/intellectual disability (DD/ID) in all affected individuals. Other common manifestations are epilepsy, muscular hypotonia, movement disorders, spasticity, feeding difficulties, and behavior issues. A subset of individuals show a malformation of cortical development consisting of extensive and diffuse bilateral polymicrogyria.\" [PMID:31219694]\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0028154\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"GRIN1-related developmental and epileptic encephalopathy\" EXACT [PMID:31219694]\nsynonym: \"GRIN1-related neurodevelopmental disorder\" EXACT [PMID:31219694]\nxref: GARD:0028154 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0700092 {source=\"PMID:31219694\"} ! neurodevelopmental disorder\nis_a: MONDO:1060138 {source=\"PMID:40374652\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163\"} ! GRIN-related complex neurodevelopmental disorder\nintersection_of: MONDO:0700092 ! neurodevelopmental disorder\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/4584 ! GRIN1\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/4584 {source=\"PMID:31219694\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163\"} ! GRIN1\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9063\" xsd:string\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060179\nname: RNU5B-1 related neurodevelopmental disorder with seizures and joint laxity\ndef: \"A neurodevelopmental disorder in which the cause of the disease is a variation in RNU5B-1 gene and is characterized by global developmental delay, hypotonia, macrocephaly, failure to thrive, abnormality of the eye, seizures, and joint laxity\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40060/, MONDO:patterns/disease_series_by_gene, PMID:40379786, PMID:40442284]\nsubset: omim {source=\"OMIM:621302\"}\nsynonym: \"NEDSJL\" EXACT ABBREVIATION [OMIM:621302]\nsynonym: \"neurodevelopmental disorder with seizures and joint laxity\" EXACT [OMIM:621302]\nsynonym: \"RNU5B-1 related neurodevelopmental disorder with seizures and joint laxity\" EXACT [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40060/] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nsynonym: \"RNU5B-1-related disorder\" BROAD [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40060/]\nxref: OMIM:621302 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0100500 {source=\"PMID:40379786\", source=\"PMID:40442284\", source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40060/\"} ! Mendelian neurodevelopmental disorder\nintersection_of: MONDO:0100500 ! Mendelian neurodevelopmental disorder\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/10212 ! RNU5B-1\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/10212 {source=\"OMIM:621302\", source=\"PMID:40379786\", source=\"PMID:40442284\", source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40060/\"} ! RNU5B-1\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator \"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\" xsd:string\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9596\" xsd:anyURI\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
